  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Productivity and Climate Resilience of Rice Cultivation in Narsingdi, Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establish a low-carbon rice value chain in the Narsingdi region of Bangladesh by intergrating Alternate Wetting and Drying (AWD) practices with a digital MRV (Measurement, Reporting, and Verification) System. Provide training to 160 smallholder farmers to support their transitoin to sustainable agriculture, increasing farm income through water savings, improved productivity, and carbon credit-based incentives enabled by solar pump adoption and AWD-based paddy water management. Strengthen local climate change response capacity through close collaboration with local partners (including BADC, BRRI, SSG, and PS PraniSheba) by supproting system installation, technical training, and on-the-ground implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In accordance with the fundamental principles of Article 3 of the Framework Act on International Development Cooperation, this project seeks to achieve sustainable development by eradicating poverty among smallholder farmers in the Narsingdi region of Bangladesh and increasing their annual household income. By introducing low-carbon rice cultivation technologies and a digital MRV (Measurement, Reporting, and Verification) system, the project simultaneously improves agricultural productivity and enhances climate change mitigation, while supporting farmer&amp;#39;s economic self-reliance through and inclusive business model. Through this approach, the project aims to establish a sustainable agriculture model in developing countries and scale it across Asia, thereby countributing to shared global prosperity and the common benefit of humanity.&#xad6c;&#xcd95;&#xb41c; &#xd6a8;&#xc728;&#xc801; &#xbb3c;&#xad00;&#xb9ac; &#xae30;&#xbc18; &#xc778;&#xd504;&#xb77c;, &#xad50;&#xc721; &#xc644;&#xb8cc;&#xb41c; &#xd604;&#xc9c0; &#xb18d;&#xbd80;, &#xac15;&#xd654;&#xb41c; &#xac04;&#xd5d0;&#xad00;&#xac1c; &#xce21;&#xc815; &#xc5ed;&#xb7c9;</narrative>
  </description>
